	(text "C64 USB-C PD Power Adapter v0.4 (DC only, no 50/60 Hz: the C64 TOD clock will not tick from mains)\nNeeds a USB-C PD charger offering 15 V. U1 (CH224A) requests 15 V via R1 = 56k.\nQ1 connects the 15 V rail only after the PD contract (PG low). U2 and U3 start only above ~13.2 V (EN UVLO),\nso a plain 5 V charger, or one that falls back to 9/12 V, never powers the C64.\nDIN 4+5 = +5.07 V: U2 -> U4 eFuse (cuts off above 5.70 V, back on below 5.18 V; 3.3 A limit), D1 TVS.\nDIN 6 = +12.3 V DC: U3 -> U5 eFuse (cuts off above 14.2 V, back on below 12.9 V; 1.5 A limit), D2 TVS, into the C64 \"9 VAC\" bridge.\nDIN 1/2/3/7 = GND. Both eFuses also block reverse current and retry automatically after a fault."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
